1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,944
Welcome. Our group presents a smart fan speed controller for the Fuzzy Logic and

2
00:00:05,944 --> 00:00:11,888
Genetic Programming subject at L. D. College of Engineering, Ahmedabad. We are four Chemical

3
00:00:11,888 --> 00:00:17,831
Engineering students from Division A. This project is a software simulation.

4
00:00:17,831 --> 00:00:24,428
Manual fan adjustment requires attention as room conditions change. A simple temperature threshold ignores

5
00:00:24,428 --> 00:00:31,025
humidity. We use two inputs to create an interpretable fan command. The fan provides

6
00:00:31,025 --> 00:00:37,622
airflow. We do not claim that it removes humidity or lowers the room temperature.

7
00:00:37,622 --> 00:00:44,334
Our objectives are to define fuzzy sets, build nine understandable rules, implement the controller,

8
00:00:44,334 --> 00:00:51,046
and test its response. A separate genetic programming experiment learns an approximation of simulated

9
00:00:51,046 --> 00:00:57,758
fuzzy outputs. We report model limitations instead of claiming measured energy savings.

10
00:00:57,758 --> 00:01:03,884
Temperature ranges from fifteen to forty degrees Celsius. Relative humidity ranges from twenty to

11
00:01:03,884 --> 00:01:10,010
ninety percent. The output is a normalized fan command from zero to one hundred

12
00:01:10,010 --> 00:01:16,136
percent. We validate, fuzzify, evaluate rules, aggregate consequents, and calculate the centroid. Hardware integration

13
00:01:16,136 --> 00:01:22,263
remains future work.

14
00:01:22,263 --> 00:01:28,806
Each variable has low, medium and high triangular memberships. Shoulder sets cover the ends

15
00:01:28,806 --> 00:01:35,350
of the domain. A reading can belong partly to more than one set. These

16
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:41,894
degrees are memberships, not probabilities. The thresholds are illustrative classroom design choices.

17
00:01:41,894 --> 00:01:46,630
The table contains nine rules. Each row is a temperature set and each column

18
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:51,367
is a humidity set. For example, medium temperature and high humidity request high fan

19
00:01:51,367 --> 00:01:56,103
speed. High temperature requests high speed at every humidity level. Every rule has equal

20
00:01:56,103 --> 00:02:00,840
weight.

21
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:06,857
The main implementation uses NumPy, so scikit fuzzy is not required. AND takes the

22
00:02:06,857 --> 00:02:12,875
minimum membership. Each output set is clipped at its rule strength. Maximum combines all

23
00:02:12,875 --> 00:02:18,892
clipped sets. Trapezoidal integration calculates the output centroid on a zero point one percentage

24
00:02:18,892 --> 00:02:24,910
point grid. Invalid inputs raise an error.

25
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:31,030
At thirty degrees, medium temperature membership is zero point seven five. At eighty percent

26
00:02:31,030 --> 00:02:37,150
humidity, high membership is zero point six. The strongest rule clips the high output

27
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:43,270
at zero point six. Medium output also activates at zero point two. Their aggregated

28
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:49,391
centroid gives a seventy three point one one three percent fan command.

29
00:02:49,391 --> 00:02:54,838
The examples span cool, moderate and warm conditions. Twenty eight degrees and sixty percent

30
00:02:54,838 --> 00:03:00,286
humidity gives fifty percent. Forty degrees and ninety percent gives about eighty three point

31
00:03:00,286 --> 00:03:05,734
three three percent. A shoulder output reaches its centroid inside its support, so the

32
00:03:05,734 --> 00:03:11,181
command does not reach one hundred percent.

33
00:03:11,181 --> 00:03:16,283
All one thousand four hundred and seventy nine validation points returned finite bounded outputs.

34
00:03:16,283 --> 00:03:21,385
The response is continuous, but it has small local decreases. On our test grid

35
00:03:21,385 --> 00:03:26,487
the largest temperature step decrease is one point three six percentage points. The largest

36
00:03:26,487 --> 00:03:31,589
humidity step decrease is two point three nine points. The report explains these centroid

37
00:03:31,589 --> 00:03:36,691
effects.

38
00:03:36,691 --> 00:03:41,874
Genetic programming evolves expression trees using addition, subtraction, multiplication, minimum and maximum. We use

39
00:03:41,874 --> 00:03:47,057
one hundred trees for forty generations with a fixed seed. Eighty five samples train

40
00:03:47,057 --> 00:03:52,240
the model and thirty six are held out. Test error is nine point four

41
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:57,423
three one percentage points against the simulated fuzzy target. This experiment does not optimize

42
00:03:57,423 --> 00:04:02,606
real comfort.

43
00:04:02,606 --> 00:04:09,234
The project demonstrates an explainable fuzzy controller and an actual genetic programming approximation. Our

44
00:04:09,234 --> 00:04:15,861
deliverables include reproducible code, graphs, a report, and this presentation. Future work includes monotonic

45
00:04:15,861 --> 00:04:22,488
response tuning and hardware calibration. Public repository, LinkedIn and video links will be added

46
00:04:22,488 --> 00:04:29,116
after the group uploads the files. Thank you.
